From 3f47f351e8c60fe6aa4b3196bdd32f76d78f50f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Al Miraj Admin Bot <admin@elm3raj.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:22:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(admin): make customer phone numbers click-to-call on
 Orders
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mobile-first tel: links for order.phone across admin Orders views:
- Compact order card (إدارة الطلبات): the phone becomes an obvious
  ≥44px tappable pill with a "اتصال" label on mobile, shrinking to a
  subtle inline link on desktop (sm+). No behavior change to the
  displayed number.
- Archive/delivery cards and the recent-orders table: phone becomes a
  clickable tel: link as well.

Tapping the phone link always stops propagation so it never triggers
the parent order card's expand/collapse click handler. hrefs are
sanitized (digits + optional leading "+") without altering the number
shown to the admin. Links carry an Arabic aria-label, and the "اتصال"
badge is hidden in print (print:hidden) so printed pages still show
the plain number.

No changes to WhatsApp integration, delivery-company logic, order
statuses, database, API/order creation, or Meta verification.
